---
// about.astro
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — staring at the ceiling" description="About staring at the ceiling.">
  <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-8">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="pb-5 border-b border-[#d8dce2] dark:border-[#333a46]">
      <h1 class="font-mono text-base font-semibold tracking-wide text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">
        About
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs font-mono text-zinc-400 dark:text-zinc-500 mt-1">
        staring at the ceiling
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Narrative Section -->
    <section class="space-y-4 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
      <p>
        I am being restless, tired then restless again. I'm being that slave of the race master, world order or whatever day by day. And it hurts. If one thing in the world that I fear is- not being me. And the world around is pushing me in that way. It's scary. And I'm scared. I know it is inevitable to escape. But least I can do is renting about it. That's why this blog exist.
      </p>
      <p>
        I sometimes stare at the ceiling and let my inner 'me' have a conversation with himself. Sometimes he sounds stupid, sometimes smart, sometimes he behaves like an annoying freak. But I do enjoy listening to him. But my never settling consciousness is unable to remember all that. I feel like letting them fade away is a big miss. Not for anybody else. But for me. You see, I like being nostalgic. God, I love being nostalgic. Probably one of my most favourite pastimes. People or events are great source of nostalgia. I get that and all. But probably the most chilling source of nostalgia is past version of oneself. Thinking about what I was doing at a particular day, how the day was always sends chills down my spine. Maybe I'm a bit self-centered. Maybe that's normal. I don't care.
      </p>
      <p>
        So, anyway, thats why I decided to create a blog, where I will dump whatever silly thoughts I have (I decided it while staring at the ceiling, ofcourse).
      </p>
      <p>
        I'll not use any in AI writing, proof reading or editing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Quick questions -->
    <section class="pt-6 border-t border-[#d8dce2] dark:border-[#333a46] space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-mono font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-400 dark:text-zinc-500">
        Quick questions:
      </h2>
      <ol class="space-y-3 text-sm sm:text-base text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
        <li class="space-y-1">
          <p class="font-medium text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">1. Who are the target audience?</p>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 pl-4">-&gt; Only me.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="space-y-1">
          <p class="font-medium text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">2. Why putting it in the web then?</p>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 pl-4">-&gt; Just in case someone is interested.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="space-y-1">
          <p class="font-medium text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">3. Will I filter out what I write ?</p>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 pl-4">-&gt; Maybe</p>
        </li>
        <li class="space-y-1">
          <p class="font-medium text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">4. How often Will I write?</p>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 pl-4">-&gt; I honestly don't know. There is a healthy chance that I will not write anything ever.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
